From: taimen camera bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: agc: protect highlights like vendor AE

The MSV controller exposes for the histogram mean alone, so a lamp or a
window in the frame gets blown out while the mean sits comfortably at
target -- the single biggest visible difference from the vendor AE.
When a meaningful share of pixels lands in the top histogram bin, bias
the measurement upward so the controller backs off and recovers the
highlights. Threshold 2% of pixels, proportional gain 12, capped at
+1.5 MSV so a genuinely bright scene cannot crash the exposure.

--- a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/agc.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/agc.cpp
@@ -190,5 +190,19 @@
 	}
 
 	float exposureMSV = (denom == 0 ? 0 : static_cast<float>(num) / denom);
+
+	/*
+	 * Highlight protection, vendor-style: if a meaningful share of the
+	 * scene sits in the top bin, bias the measurement upward so the
+	 * controller backs off and recovers the highlights rather than
+	 * exposing for the mean alone.
+	 */
+	if (denom != 0) {
+		float topFrac = static_cast<float>(
+			exposureBins[kExposureBinsCount - 1]) / denom;
+		if (topFrac > 0.02f)
+			exposureMSV += std::min((topFrac - 0.02f) * 12.0f, 1.5f);
+	}
+
 	updateExposure(context, frameContext, exposureMSV);
 }
